{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 exit / Phase 2 test design\n\nCaller-dependency sweep: expected post-fix behavior is that every assert_nodes_do_not_mutate_external_store child owns a private basetemp and never performs pytest retention cleanup in the user-global root. The complete caller set is tests/unit/test_test_suite_store_isolation.py plus the two cases in tests/unit/test_test_suite_store_isolation_heldout.py. All three depend only on child return status and the ambient tracker HEAD/directory invariants; temp-root location is incidental. No behavioral dependency blocks repair.\n\nTest contract card:\nauthoritative_contract: tests/unit/test_test_suite_store_isolation.py:8-14 and tests/_store_isolation.py:19-46 require the selected node to complete within the bounded child run without changing ambient tracker HEAD/directories.\ntrigger_preconditions: PYTEST_DEBUG_TEMPROOT contains unlocked numbered pytest-0..pytest-3 directories; a sentinel in a cleanup-eligible directory proves the dangerous shared state exists.\nproduction_path: assert_nodes_do_not_mutate_external_store -> real captured Python/pytest subprocess -> pytest temp-path session-finish cleanup.\ntest_tier: parent/child subprocess; one tier lower cannot exercise pytest session-finish or global numbered-root selection.\nobservable_postcondition: the helper returns successfully, the exact sentinel and shared numbered-directory set remain unchanged, and the helper's existing ambient tracker assertions pass.\nci_gate: collected/executed by the default unit suite and make test.\nnegative_control: the defect-seeded mutation is omission of the private --basetemp; the fixture precondition plus the current RED deletion gives the contrast without a timing oracle.\ncollateral_invariants: ambient tracker HEAD and directory set remain exact (existing helper); unrelated shared pytest sentinel bytes and entries remain exact.\nfault_injection: real cleanup-eligible numbered pytest directories under an isolated PYTEST_DEBUG_TEMPROOT; no sleeps or mocked cleanup."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786891225395284001,"uuid":"a1f35aed-1180-4007-b1a5-113700d9d82e"}